      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Was going to make separate request, but it seems related. I also have need for muscle offsets in avatar (humanoid rigging) settings, because there are problems with lowering shoulders too much in vr mode with my avatar. And i can't find any useful solution to that other than changing bone positions and re-weight-painiting whole shoulder-chest piece of model.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-12T23:15:11.413Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Vrchat currently does not seem to use any of the eye range or eye offset configurations I have stored in the humanoid mapper. Vrchat really needs to use them because the eyes on my avatars will rotate too much, sometimes be flipped backward, and be incorrectly offset due to how it seems to directly assign bone orientation. The angles should at the least be offset by the eye's rest rotation and clamped by the eyes range.",
